    <string name="rel_2_0_3_a">Bug fixes</string>
    <string name="rel_2_0_3_b">Battery usage optimization</string>
    <string name="rel_2_0_2_a">New floating navigation bar</string>
    <string name="rel_2_0_2_b">Line thickness is chosen for each track, along with its color</string>
    <string name="rel_2_0_1_a">The position dot is blue again</string>
    <string name="rel_2_0_a">Interface redesign</string>
    <string name="rel_1_3_1_a">Several security flaws fixed</string>
    <string name="rel_1_3_a">Reduced battery consumption</string>
    <string name="rel_1_2_a">A security flaw fixed</string>
    <string name="rel_1_1_a">Map loading is much faster, especially in satellite view</string>
    <string name="rel_1_1_b">The CSV conversion tool has been removed</string>
    <string name="rel_1_0_a">First stable version</string>
    <string name="rel_2_1_0_a">The application follows the phone\'s language, in 11 languages</string>
    <string name="rel_2_1_0_b">Release notes are shown in your language</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_13_a">The debug log takes up less space: 50 MB at most</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_12_a">New debug log: it notes what happens in the application to help find the cause of a problem (200 MB at most)</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_12_b">Settings: “Debug log” to share, save or clear it</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_11_a">Trash: emptying the trash really frees up space on the phone, even when it is almost full</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_11_b">The trash now keeps only about 500 MB: beyond that, the oldest deleted tracks are erased</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_10_a">All maps zoom as far as the main map, up to level 21</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_10_b">Split: “Show other tracks” is in the same place as in Extend, under the chosen track</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_9_a">Main map: an arrow above “Focus position” unfolds a magnifier, to search for an address or a city and go there</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_9_b">Split: “Show other tracks” draws other tracks in the background to find your bearings</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_8_a">The app\'s maps are synchronized: a tool opens where the main map was looking, at the same zoom</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_8_b">Extend: “Show other tracks” draws other tracks in the background to find your bearings</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_7_a">The trash can be emptied in one go, after a three-second warning</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_6_a">Extend: touch the track anywhere, even right in the middle, then draw the continuation</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_6_b">Split opens on the map, without the “By segment” mode; the portion is placed more precisely and the track no longer disappears when zooming</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_6_c">City search on the tools\' maps</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_6_d">A track modified by a tool stays displayed on the map</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_6_e">KML export is much lighter, like Google Earth\'s</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_5_a">Long press on a track on the map to delete that piece (the old track goes to the trash)</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_5_b">Split opens directly on “On the map”</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_5_c">The split map keeps the tracks\' original colors</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_4_a">Split on the map: an “Undo point” button to redo a misplaced point without leaving the map</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_4_b">The map zoom is kept when the tool is reopened on the same track</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_3_a">Split on the map cuts exactly where the track was touched, even between two distant points</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_3_b">KML export keeps the thickness chosen for the track, otherwise that of the original file</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_2_a">KML export returns a Google Earth file as it was on import: same folders, same track names, same colors and thicknesses (re-import files already imported)</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_2_b">The Trash button stays visible even when the history is empty</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_1_a">Trash: a deleted track stays there for 30 days and can be restored from the history, then erases itself</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_1_c">KML export keeps the track\'s colors, segment by segment, instead of making everything red</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_1_b">The “Trim” tool is removed: “Split”, “On the map” mode, does the same thing</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_a">New “Extend” tool: draw on the map the missing part of a track stopped too early, at the end or at the start, by touching the map point after point</string>
    <string name="rel_2_3_b">“Split”, “On the map” mode: the track\'s detail follows the zoom, you place the start then the end with a tap, and the result fits in a single track</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_5_a">“Split”, “On the map” mode: the result now fits in a single track, with no line across the removed portion</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_5_b">The original is deleted by default in this mode (the switch is still there to keep it)</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_4_a">“Split”, “On the map” mode: the map shows the track\'s detail when you zoom, no longer cutting corners</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_4_b">You place the start then the end of the portion with a tap on the map, instead of sliders</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_3_a">“Split”, “On the map” mode: no more line between points that nothing links</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_2_a">“Clean up” keeps the exact shape of the track: only the GPS scribble left in place becomes one point, without cutting the line</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_2_b">History: a selection mode (“Select”, or long press) to select all, show, hide, merge or delete several tracks at once</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_2_c">“Split”: new “On the map” mode to remove the portion of your choice</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_2_d">The GPS signal found or lost unfolds from the small status dot</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_1_a">“Clean up” reduces each stop to a single point, without cutting the track, and keeps everything else intact</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_a">New “Clean up” tool: removes the points piled up in the same place when the recording kept going</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_b">The thickest tracks are drawn under the thinnest</string>
    <string name="rel_2_2_c">The application is entirely in French again</string>
